<p>The concept is great but poor execution. The interview bugged me until I noticed it was conducted by a field agent, presumably undercover: a note clarifying would be nice. But there's a lot of cleanup to do, too. For instance:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Any identified instances of SCP-2809-1 are to be administered amnestics <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">sufficient to remove any memories associated with SCP-2809.</span></p>
</blockquote>
<p>The part I struck through part could just be deleted.</p>
<p>Also, since it's implied that the Foundation has yet to intercept an instance of SCP-2809-1 before the trip, a lot of the detail regarding how they're picked up etc. should probably be omitted. Maybe a note can be given about them not appearing on any airport security cameras.</p>

